'''''Bloomberg Technology''''', formerly called '''''Bloomberg West''''', is an American television show produced by [[Bloomberg Television]]. Andy Lack, [[chief executive officer]] (CEO) of Bloomberg Media Group launched ''Bloomberg West'' in 2011.<ref name=BOSTONIA>{{cite news|title=News Without End|url=https://www.bu.edu/bostonia/summer11/bloomberg/bloomberg.pdf|accessdate=25 July 2011|newspaper=BOSTONIA|date=Summer 2011}}</ref>

The show focused on the topics of technology, innovation, and business and was hosted by [[Emily Chang (journalist)|Emily Chang]] and Cory Johnson.<ref name=TechCrunch>{{cite news|last=Arrington|first=Michael|title=Bloomberg Launching Daily Live Tech TV Show Called Bloomberg West On Monday|url=https://techcrunch.com/2011/02/25/bloomberg-launching-daily-live-tech-tv-show-called-bloomberg-west-on-monday/|accessdate=25 July 2011|newspaper=TechCrunch|date=February 25, 2011}}</ref>
Before coming to Bloomberg Television, Chang was a [[CNN]] television host in [[Beijing]]. Co-host Cory Johnson, ran a hedge fund and reported on [[Silicon Valley]] for [[CNBC]] before joining Bloomberg Television.<ref name=Reynolds>{{cite news|last=Phillips|first=Robin J|title=Bloomberg launches West Coast show from San Francisco|url=http://businessjournalism.org/2011/02/28/bloomberg-launches-west-coast-show-from-san-francisco/|accessdate=25 July 2011|newspaper=Reynolds Center|date=Feb 28, 2011|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://archive.today/20130414120012/http://businessjournalism.org/2011/02/28/bloomberg-launches-west-coast-show-from-san-francisco/|archive-date=14 April 2013}}</ref>

From its start in 2011, the show has been recorded in Bloomberg’s San Francisco Pier 3 studio<ref name="propminc/bloomberg">{{cite web |title=Bloomberg LP (BLP), West Coast Offices & Broadcast Studio Pier 3 San Francisco, California |url=http://propminc.com/pro_bloomberg_lp.html |website=ProPM Inc. |access-date=5 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170501193411/http://propminc.com/pro_bloomberg_lp.html |archive-date=1 May 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Bloomberg updates West Coast studio |url=https://www.newscaststudio.com/2015/10/07/bloomberg-updates-west-coast-studio/ |access-date=5 January 2023 |work=NewscastStudio}}</ref><ref name="businessinsider/bloomberg-west">{{cite news |last1=Rosoff |first1=Matt |title=An Inside Look At Bloomberg's Beautiful West Coast Offices |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/a-inside-look-at-bloombergs-beautiful-west-coast-offices-2011-6 |access-date=5 January 2023 |work=Business Insider}}</ref> and aired daily at 6:00pm EST.<ref name=Reynolds/>

''Bloomberg West'' was named ''Bloomberg Technology'' as part of the launch of Bloomberg Technology as a "multi-platform brand" on October 5, 2016.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.adweek.com/news/television/bloomberg-announces-new-multiplatform-brand-tech-news-173906|title=Bloomberg Announces New Multiplatform Brand for Tech News|last=Main|first=Sami|date=October 5, 2016|newspaper=AdWeek|access-date=2016-10-13}}</ref>

In August 16, 2024, Bloomberg Technology is ceased broadcasting at 11:56 am (NY) and is change name to Style It Out at 11am (SGT).

